  "Question": "One proposal for new postage rates for a letter was \\(30\\)¢ for the first ounce and \\(22\\)¢ for each additional ounce (or fraction of an ounce). The postage for a letter weighing \\(4.5\\) ounces was",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(96\\)¢",
    "B": "\\(\\$1.07\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\$1.18\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\$1.20\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\$1.40\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The first ounce costs \\(30\\) cents. After that ounce, the remaining weight is \\(4.5-1=3.5\\) ounces. This includes three full additional ounces and part of a fourth. Because a fraction of an ounce receives a full additional-ounce charge, there are four charges of \\(22\\) cents.\n\nThe postage is therefore\n\\[\n30+4\\cdot22=30+88=118\n\\]\ncents, or \\(\\$1.18\\), choice C.",
